{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563179,"nonce":"LA0JxhbmsKig3B1EUGUiv2RUafo=","title":"Canvas: a 2D drawing context on top of registerCanvas","message":"Today a canvas is a raw GPU callback (registerCanvas with a CanvasFrame). Keep that as the extension point, and add the drawing context most canvases want, as ashui's DrawContext: transforms, clips (rect, rounded rect, circle, path) and opacity as stacks; fill and stroke of rects, circles and paths with solid, gradient and pattern brushes; images; text; redrawing only when what it read changes.\n\nGeometry comes from blinc_abi a023766 (paths, flattening, tessellation and strokes in Rust, shared with ashui), and the path shader is a port of ashui's PathShader. A framework or an app can still drop to the GPU callback for its own pipelines, mixed with the drawing context in one canvas.","files":null}]}